  "body": "# Associated User Story\n\nAs an officer, I want the sign in/up page to only show an option to sign in/up, and no other details.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n**The sign in/up page shows only the sign in and sign up options, with no member data, points, events, or other organization details visible before login.**\n\n- Sunny: A visitor opens the site and sees only the sign in and sign up options. No points, member names, events, or dashboard information appear on the page. After signing in, the user is taken to their dashboard, where the appropriate details are shown based on their role.\n\n- Rainy: A visitor who isn't logged in tries to open a dashboard, member record, or other internal page directly by its link, or the sign in page fails to load. The system redirects them to the sign in/up page, or shows a clear message (e.g., \"Please sign in to continue\" or \"Try again later or contact an officer\") instead of a blank page or exposing any details. No member information is visible without signing in.\n\n\n\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
